# Riku of Many Paths: "Whenever you cast a modal spell, choose up to X, where X is the number of times you chose a mode for that
# spell" (CR 700.2, 603.3c). Turn 1: Riku comes down with Mox Emerald, Mox Sapphire and Mox Ruby. Turn 3: Kolaghan's Command with
# two modes gives X = 2, so three modes are refused beside two chosen: the top card (Ornithopter) is exiled and a 1/1 blue flying
# Bird is made; Ornithopter, cast from exile, is no modal spell and triggers nothing. Turn 4: Bot2's Boros Charm is not Bot1's spell,
# and Bot1's Holy Day in response to it is no modal spell either (the last modal spell cast was Bot2's): no trigger. Turn 5: Boros
# Charm with one mode gives X = 1, so only the counter-and-trample mode is taken (two are refused): Riku is a 4/4 with trample.

